/.venv
/converted_mods
/manual_steps
/uv.lock
/Faerun
/refs
*.pyc
*.egg-info
__pycache__/

# Derived from refs/atlas_nations_1371_guide_map.png (copyrighted, gitignored).
# The overlay traces the atlas coastline, so it stays local like its source;
# regenerate with `uv run python scripts/measure_faerun_scale.py`.
docs/evidence/atlas_overlay.png
# measurement caches, regenerated by scripts/measure_*.py
docs/evidence/*.npz
# Every CLI run rewrites this, so a tracked copy is pure churn.
# NOTE for the coordinator: it is still in the index -> `git rm --cached
# docs/evidence/last_run.md` in the commit that lands this line.
docs/evidence/last_run.md
# The whole-mod ck3-tiger report is 359 MB (208k warnings, one block each).
# The committed extract is tiger_full_<date>_summary.txt: every error/fatal
# block plus the by-kind summary. Regenerate the full one with
# scripts/validate_output_mod.sh.
docs/evidence/tiger_full_*.txt
!docs/evidence/tiger_full_*_summary.txt
# Full-run nohup logs (docs/evidence/full_run_*.log) - the durable record
# is docs/evidence/full_run_<date>.md.
docs/evidence/full_run_*.log
# nohup logs of long conversion runs; the durable record is
# docs/evidence/last_run.md and docs/evidence/map_build_report.json
docs/evidence/cli_full_run.log
docs/evidence/map_build_full.log
# Per-duchy barony review sheets: 979 PNGs, ~40 MB, regenerated by
# scripts/barony_review_sheets.py. index.md and the samples it names are
# committed; the rest are not (docs/step_map_baronies.md §8).
docs/evidence/baronies/*.png
!docs/evidence/baronies/d_waterdeep.png
!docs/evidence/baronies/d_menzoberranzan.png
!docs/evidence/baronies/d_the_stormstars.png
!docs/evidence/baronies/d_nelanther_isles.png
!docs/evidence/baronies/d_baldurs_gate.png
docs/evidence/barony_sheets.log
docs/evidence/map_baronies_full.log
